    "q-212662": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212662",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let $A={0,4,5}$ and consider the relation \"is equal to\" $(=)$ on $A.$  If this relation is given by the set $R,$ express $R$ as a set of ordered pairs.\n\n$R={(0,0),(4,$\n{{field-1}}$),($\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$)}$",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}$ such that $x=y.$\n\nLet's check each element $x\\in A$ to see which elements $y\\in A$ it could be paired with to satisfy the relation.\n\n- If $x=0,$ then the value $y=0$ satisfies $x=y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(0,0).$\n\n- If $x=4,$ then the value $y=4$ satisfies $x=y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(4,4).$\n\n- If $x=5,$ then the value $y=5$ satisfies $x=y.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(5,5).$\n\nTherefore, we can describe our relation as the following set of ordered pairs:\n\n$$\nR={(0,0),(4,4),(5,5)}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
