    "q-212996": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212996",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Let $A={2,5}$ and consider the relation \"are congruent modulo $3$\" on $A.$ Write out $R$ as a set of ordered pairs.",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}$ such that $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3).$\n\nLet's check each element $x\\in A$ to see which elements $y\\in A$ it could be paired with to satisfy the relation.\n\n- If $x=2,$ then the values $y=2$ and $y=5$ satisfy $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3),$ since $3∣(2-2)$ and $3∣(2-5).$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(2,2),(2,5).$\n\n- If $x=5,$ then the values $y=2$ and $y=5$ satisfy $x≡y\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3),$ since $3∣(5-2)$ and $3∣(5-5).$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(5,2),(5,5).$\n\nTherefore, we can describe our relation as the following set of ordered pairs:\n\n$$\nR={(2,2),(2,5),(5,2),(5,5)}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
