    "q-213003": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213003",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA={{0},{1,0}}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following ordered pairs is an element of the relation \"is **not** a subset of\" on $A?$ \n\n- $({0},{1,0})$\n- $({1,0},{0})$\n- $({1,0},{1,0})$",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}$ such that $x⊈y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our ordered pairs in turn.\n\n- The ordered pair $({0},{1,0})$ is **not** an element of $R$ since ${0}⊆{1,0}.\\,\\times $\n\n- The ordered pair $({1,0},{0})$ is an element of $R$ since ${1,0}⊈{0}.\\,✓$\n\n- The ordered pair $({1,0},{1,0})$ is **not** an element of $R$ since ${1,0}⊆{1,0}.\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
