    "q-212987": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212987",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "Let $B={2,3,4}.$ Which set is equivalent to the following relation on $B?$\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {B}^{2}\\,:\\,6∣xy}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {B}^{2}$ such that $6∣xy.$\n\nLet's check each element $x\\in B$ to see which elements $y\\in B$ it could be paired with to satisfy the conditions of our relation.\n\n- If $x=2,$ then the value $y=3$ satisfies $6∣xy.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(2,3).$\n\n- If $x=3,$ then the values $y=2,4$ satisfy $6∣xy.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(3,2)$ and $(3,4).$\n\n- If $x=4,$ then the value $y=3$ satisfies $6∣xy.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(4,3).$\n\nTherefore, we can describe our relation as the following set of ordered pairs:\n\n$$\nR={(2,3),(3,2),(3,4),(4,3)}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
