    "q-85991": {
      "dom_id": "step-q85991",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Let $B={0,1,2,3,4}.$ Which set is equivalent to the following relation on $B?$\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {B}^{2}\\,:\\,y=2x}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {B}^{2}$ such that $y=2x.$\n\nLet's check each element $x\\in B$ to see which elements $y\\in B$ it could be paired with to satisfy the conditions of our relation.\n\n- If $x=0,$  then the value $y=0$ satisfies $y=2x.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(0,0).$\n\n- If $x=1,$ then the value $y=2$ satisfies $y=2x.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair  $(1,2).$\n\n- If $x=2,$ then the value $y=4$ satisfies $y=2x.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair  $(2,4).$\n\n- If $x=3,$  then there is no value of $y\\in B$ that satisfies $y=2x.$\n\n- If $x=4,$ then there is no value of $y\\in B$ that satisfies $y=2x.$\n\nTherefore, we can describe our relation as the following set of ordered pairs:\n\n$$\nR={(0,0),(1,2),(2,4)}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-85991-a",
