    "q-212680": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212680",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Let $B={2,4}.$ Which set is equivalent to the following relation on $B?$\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {B}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ne 2x}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {B}^{2}$ such that $y\\ne 2x.$\n\nLet's check each element $x\\in B$ to see which elements $y\\in B$ it could be paired with to satisfy the conditions of our relation.\n\n- If $x=2,$  then the value $y=2$ satisfies $y\\ne 2x.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(2,2).$\n\n- If $x=4,$ then the values $y=2$ and $y=4$ satisfy $y\\ne 2x.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(4,2)$ and $(4,4).$\n\nTherefore, we can describe our relation as the following set of ordered pairs:\n\n$$\nR={(2,2),(4,2),(4,4)}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
